# Component CSS

Styles use **Tailwind CSS 4** and **daisyUI 5**. Entry: `src/styles/main.css`.

## Setup

1. Vite plugin `@tailwindcss/vite` is first in `vite.config.ts`.
2. `src/main.ts` imports `@/styles/main.css` once.
3. daisyUI ships `light` and `dark`. Switch with `data-theme` on `<html>`.

### Required: `@reference` in scoped styles

Every `<style scoped>` that uses `@apply` MUST start with a `@reference` to the entry stylesheet (not bare `"tailwindcss"`), so daisyUI utilities resolve:

```vue
<style scoped>
@reference "@/styles/main.css";

.animal-card {
  @apply card bg-base-100 shadow-sm;
}
</style>
```

`@/` maps to `src/` (Vite + `tsconfig.app.json`).

## Principles

### Semantic classes + `@apply`

Keep templates readable. Move repeated or long utility clusters into `<style scoped>`.

**Bad:** `class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 rounded-lg border px-4 py-3 bg-base-100"`

**Good:** `class="animal-card"` + `@apply` in CSS.

Inline utilities are fine when they are local layout helpers (`flex`, `gap-2`, `w-full`) and do not repeat.

### Naming (component-scoped)

- Root: `.animal-card`
- Sections: `.animal-card-header`, `.animal-card-body`
- States: `.animal-card--adopted`, `.animal-card-item--selected`

Name the **role**, not the look (`.status-badge`, not `.blue-box`).

### daisyUI usage

- Prefer daisyUI semantic colors (`bg-base-100`, `text-base-content`, `bg-primary`). Do not use `dark:` with daisyUI color names.
- Use documented variants only (`btn-primary`, `badge-error`). Do not invent classes like `badge-base-300`.
- Default variant unless a color/size was requested (`btn`, not `btn btn-primary`).
- `modal-box` stays in the template — never recreate it with `@apply`.

### Organization inside `<style scoped>`

1. `@reference`
2. Root
3. Layout
4. Elements
5. Modifiers / states
6. Responsive (mobile-first, inside `@apply`)

## Checklist

- [ ] `@reference "@/styles/main.css"` is first in every `<style scoped>` that uses `@apply`
- [ ] Semantic class names in the template; utilities in CSS when they repeat
- [ ] daisyUI semantic colors; no invented variants
- [ ] Modifiers use `--` (`--adopted`, `--selected`)
